<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:32:default:windows">
<!--
    A fixed-frame caller that re-reserves what a __stdcall import popped keeps
    its frame offsets (`option calleepopframe on|off`), and a C runtime import
    is __cdecl.

    Issue: GH Noelo-Lab/kuna#1029. MinGW's GetSpecialFolder(path, folder)
    writes every call's arguments with `mov [esp+k]` and lowers ESP again after
    each advapi32 call (`call [RegOpenKeyExA]; sub esp,0x14`). 0x401000 is the
    same shape: memset(path) through a `jmp [msvcrt!memset]` thunk, then
    RegOpenKeyExA(HKCU, ..., &key), RegQueryValueExA(key, folder, 0, 0, path,
    &size) and RegCloseKey(key) on both paths.

    Stage / sub-stage: P6 stack-pointer-flow (`StackSolver::build`'s guessed
    equation for an unknown extrapop, `p6_variables/kuna_calleepopframe.rs`),
    with the C runtime import declared `__cdecl` at the analysis commit
    (`loader/pe_iat.rs (c_runtime_import_names)`).

    P0 assertion: `option calleepopframe on|off` (on by default, under
    `calleepop`).

    The fixture `calleepopframe_pe_i386.exe` is assembled from
    `calleepopframe_pe_i386.asm` (see the fixtures README).

    Pass 1 (`option calleepopframe off`) reproduces the BUG: with no push run
    the RegOpenKeyExA/RegQueryValueExA guesses stay at 4, each `sub` lowers the
    solved ESP, the `folder` argument becomes a local passed uninitialized and
    both RegCloseKey calls take the size buffer instead of the key.
    Pass 2 (default) is the FIX: two parameters, the key RegOpenKeyExA filled
    is the one queried and closed, and `folder` is forwarded. memset keeps its
    argument in both passes; read as __stdcall it would pop 12 bytes and move
    the key slot in pass 2 as well.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/calleepopframe_pe_i386.exe</com>
  <com>option calleepopframe off</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load addr 0x401000</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/calleepopframe_pe_i386.exe</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load addr 0x401000</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="CALLEEPOPFRAME #1: off drops the folder parameter" min="1" max="1">sub_401000\(void \*a0\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="CALLEEPOPFRAME #2: off closes the size buffer" min="2" max="2">RegCloseKey\(v5\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="CALLEEPOPFRAME #3: on keeps both parameters" min="1" max="1">sub_401000\(void \*a0,unsigned int a1\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="CALLEEPOPFRAME #4: on hands RegOpenKeyExA the key slot" min="1" max="1">RegOpenKeyExA\(0x80000001,"[^"]*",0,1,&amp;v3\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="CALLEEPOPFRAME #5: on queries the key with the forwarded folder" min="1" max="1">RegQueryValueExA\(v3,a1,0,0,v1,v4\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="CALLEEPOPFRAME #6: on closes the key" min="2" max="2">RegCloseKey\(v3\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="CALLEEPOPFRAME #7: memset keeps its arguments in both passes" min="2" max="2">memset\(a0,0,0x104\);</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
